outro: 1
style: gospel
guide: ooh
year: 1907
attribution: African-American spiritual from oral tradition, first printed in the 1900s (Folk Songs of the American Negro, 1907; Religious Folk Songs of the Negro, 1909); the Christmas verse "While shepherds kept their watching" is by John Wesley Work Jr., who died in 1925. Melody and words are public domain worldwide.
source_url: https://abcnotation.com/tunePage?a=trillian.mit.edu/~jc/music/abc/mirror/musicaviva.com/tunes/usa/go-tell-it-on-the/0000
tags: christmas, spiritual, gospel, carol, singalong
